1659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 802 0 R
/E (Big-O notation describes the maximum \(worst-case\) time or space complexity of an algorithm. It provides a strict upper bound, meaning the algorithm will never perform worse than the complexity represented by its Big-O notation, even for very large input sizes.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [7]
>>
